1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,256
When a critical software or creative

2
00:00:02,256 --> 00:00:04,136
project falls behind schedule,

3
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:06,893
adding three helpful teammates almost always

4
00:00:06,893 --> 00:00:09,087
pushes the finish line even further

5
00:00:09,087 --> 00:00:09,400
away.

6
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,265
In his 1975 classic The Mythical Man-Month,

7
00:00:12,265 --> 00:00:15,396
IBM engineering manager Fred Brooks showed why:

8
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:17,994
communication channels scale by N times

9
00:00:17,994 --> 00:00:19,393
N minus one over two.

10
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:21,524
Three builders have three links;

11
00:00:21,524 --> 00:00:22,990
ten create forty-five.

12
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:25,633
Every newcomer requires onboarding from your

13
00:00:25,633 --> 00:00:27,735
busiest builders right when time is

14
00:00:27,735 --> 00:00:28,275
scarcest,

15
00:00:28,275 --> 00:00:31,398
turning productive creation hours into status calls,

16
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:31,939
handoffs,

17
00:00:31,939 --> 00:00:33,140
and merge conflicts.

18
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,603
When a deadline slips,

19
00:00:34,603 --> 00:00:37,330
resist throwing headcount at the problem.

20
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:38,926
Cut non-essential scope,

21
00:00:38,926 --> 00:00:42,385
shield a tiny two-to-three-person pod from meetings,

22
00:00:42,385 --> 00:00:44,380
and ship the core asset first.

23
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:46,594
Shrink scope before expanding headcount,

24
00:00:46,594 --> 00:00:48,919
because tiny aligned pods out-ship crowded

25
00:00:48,919 --> 00:00:50,690
committees every single quarter.
